### Lab 8: Transaction-like cart workflow (operations are separate writes)
### 1. Create cart
curl -i -X PUT http://127.0.0.1:8098/buckets/cart_workflow/keys/U201 \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{"user_id":"U201","items":[{"product_id":"P10","quantity":1,"price":250}],"total":250}'

### 2. Update item quantity
curl -i -X PUT http://127.0.0.1:8098/buckets/cart_workflow/keys/U201 \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{"user_id":"U201","items":[{"product_id":"P10","quantity":3,"price":250}],"total":750}'

### 3. Retrieve final cart
curl -i http://127.0.0.1:8098/buckets/cart_workflow/keys/U201

### Discussion: these writes are not one atomic multi-key transaction. A crash between writes can leave an intermediate state.
